[1m[38;5;231mHow long should the stored identity survive?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mlocalStorage (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mSurvives browser restart, shared across tabs. Store userId only, never a raw token.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m sessionStorage
     [38;5;246mCleared when the tab closes; per-tab isolation and a smaller XSS blast radius.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m HttpOnly cookie
     [38;5;246mSet by the login response, unreadable by JS. Safest, but needs the backend that doesn't exist yet.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m In-memory only
     [38;5;246mA module variable, lost on refresh. Simplest, but does not actually persist.[39m
